<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Momin Khan I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1743</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Mirza Ja'far Najm-ud-daula</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Momin Khan I, born Mirza Ja'far Najm-ud-daula, was a Mughal official of Persian descent who founded the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khambhat">Cambay</a>, now Khambhat, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>. Posted to Cambay in the 1720s, he made it his family's hereditary seat as Mughal power declined, and he was later named governor of Gujarat. His descendants ruled Cambay as nawabs under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> and then British supremacy until 1948.</p></div>
